{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 80,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Flying business class on a U.S. airline is \na luxury in name only. After doing it once,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5120,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "most people learn to never pay cash \nfor it again. More often than not,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8640,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you deal with mushy food and grumpy attendants \nwho take every request like a personal offense. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13680,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But take a flight on a leading Asian airline and \nit’s like stepping foot into a different planet,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18240,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where every passenger, even in economy, gets \nmetal cutlery, hot towels, Haagen-Dahz, and prompt  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24640,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "service from attentive, attractive attendants who \nkneel down to your eye level whenever you speak.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29680,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it's impossible to ignore the extravagance in \nthe premium cabins, where passengers can sleep on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34480,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "beds in private suites, indulge in caviar, \nsip vintage wines, and feast on lobster and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39920,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wagyu steak. Even if you only ever fly economy \n- there is a sense of pride among the staff and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45360,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a remarkable degree of thoughtfulness built into \nevery leading Asian airline. Restrooms get cleaned  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50640,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mid-flight, every seat is built with lumbar \nsupport and adjustable footrests, plush pillows  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55680,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and thick blankets are given out to all, rather \nthan rationed, and every meal is meticulously  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60640,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "engineered for quality and presentation.\nIn contrast, the U.S. airline experience  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65440,
    "dDurationMs": 7520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is soulless— cabin crews spend more time in the \ngalley on their phones than with passengers and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72960,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "slam down trays of slop like they're feeding \ncattle. Meals are outsourced to industrial  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77680,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "caterers at the cheapest possible cost and \nget served with less care than a high school  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82160,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cafeteria. The difference is not just in the \nproduct itself, but in the sense of care and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86640,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "intention behind it. Once you experience a premium \nAsian carrier, it’s difficult to go back to U.S.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92080,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "airlines. As a result, Americans today save \nup their cash and points for seats on foreign  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97440,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "carriers simply because the domestic product is \nrarely - if ever - worth the cost. The strangest  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103440,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "part is that U.S. airlines pull in billions more \nin revenue and absolute profit than nearly every  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108480,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "other carrier on planet earth. Why can't they \noffer this kind of service and care? Is it greed,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113520,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or is it culture? It's the same industry, the \nsame business model, the same planes flying the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118800,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "same routes — so how could the experiences be \nworlds apart? How does an airline that treats  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123600,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you worse somehow make more money doing it?\nThe popular narrative is that Asian airlines  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128240,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are only able to achieve this level of hospitality \nand luxury because of state support. The argument  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134000,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "goes that these experiences are all artificially \nsubsidized by their countries, who pump billions  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138800,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into their carriers and airports to attract \ntourists - whereas the fully privatized,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143200,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for-profit, independent U.S. airlines are forced \nto make do with none of these handouts. In this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148640,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "episode, we analyze every leading Asian \nairline to break down the market dynamics  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152880,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that have uniquely enabled these international \ncarriers to outclass their American rivals  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157440,
    "dDurationMs": 7440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over decades in product, service, and standards.\nFlying in the U.S. has become a taxing experience,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164880,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where the cramped seats and rough service all \ndrive this feeling where passengers are treated as  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169360,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "costs to be minimized, rather than human beings.\nEven though every airline gets you from Point A to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174640,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Point B, who you choose makes all the difference.\nThe same is true for mental health,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179040,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where there are a lot of options \non paper that do the same thing. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182160,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there’s a tremendous difference between \nbeing processed and being genuinely cared for. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186320,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Therapy taught us to write down \nour worries on a list for later. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189280,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Our brain learns to let them go instead \nof tossing and turning all night and we  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192960,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "get up the next day, ready to problem-solve.\nLet’s be real - the hardest hurdle for most  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197680,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people with therapy is not therapy \nitself, but instead getting started. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201280,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Finding a professional that you trust, \nfiguring out the logistics, matching your  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205360,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "schedule with theirs, and then worrying before \na session if they’re even the right fit for you. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209760,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This friction is what makes people put off \ntherapy or try it once and never do it again. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214400,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "BetterHelp, the sponsor of today’s video, \nis built to remove exactly this pain point. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218800,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You start by taking a short quiz about what \nyou're looking for, and get matched with a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222720,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "licensed therapist quickly, no more endless \nbrowsing, cold-calling offices, or waitlists. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227840,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From there, you connect however you're \nmost comfortable: phone, video, or text,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232400,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whatever fits your life and comfort level.\nAnd the best part is that if it's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236240,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not the right fit, you can switch \ntherapists anytime at no extra cost. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240320,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No awkward conversations, no nagging \nfollow-ups, and no starting over from  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 244400,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "scratch — you just keep going until you \nfind the right professional who clicks. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248400,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This flexibility is a big reason why \nover 6 million people have gotten help  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252320,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through BetterHelp to date, and why their app \nholds a 4.8 out of 5 rating on the App Store. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257760,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you've been telling yourself you'll get to \nPoint B eventually, BetterHelp is the easiest,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262160,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "smoothest, and most comfortable version \nof arriving at your destination. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 266000,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Click the link in the description, or go to \nbetterhelp.com slash modernmba and get 10% off  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271520,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your first month of therapy. That's betterhelp.com \nslash modernmba for 10% off your first month. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273040,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thank you to BetterHelp for supporting \nModern MBA and making this episode possible. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278880,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To understand the global passenger aviation \nbusiness - we must first understand credit  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283280,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cards. Credit cards are an uniquely American \nphenomenon and as a result, they provide U.S.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287360,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "airlines a financial advantage that no other \ncarrier in the world gets. The co-branded  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292560,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "credit card mileage programs generate billions \nof dollars in pure profit every year for America  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296880,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "major American airlines. Whether it’s Delta’s \nand American Express or United and Chase,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301280,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the deals are all the same - these airlines \nsell virtual miles at no cost to banks every  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 305440,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "year in exchange for billions upfront. These \nbanks then dangle those same miles to consumers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 310640,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as incentives for credit card signups \nand spending. The reality is that if we  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315040,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "strip out credit card revenue, the entire U.S. \nairline industry effectively collapses. Every  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320240,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "major carrier today is already losing money \nflying passengers from Point A to Point B.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325440,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But once you add credit card revenue, these \nsame airlines instantly return to profit  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 329680,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the cash to fund operations, make payroll, \npay debt, and keep planes in the air. In short,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333840,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "credit card revenue is not a bonus, but \na critical lifeline for U.S. airlines."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 339360,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This difference is why smaller carriers like \nFrontier and Southwest are struggling and a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343840,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "big reason why Spirit today is bankrupt. They \ngenerate far less cash from credit cards and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 349040,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thus must ruthlessly squeeze every penny out \nof passengers to offset their growing costs.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353600,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From this angle, the goal of every major \nU.S. airline is to pull you into their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 357520,
    "dDurationMs": 914,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ecosystem. The more you swipe with their card, \nthe more miles they can sell and the more you fly,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358434,
    "dDurationMs": 2046,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the more valuable these miles will be to you. \nThat way, you’ll fly with them no matter what  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360480,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because you want the points. Throw in \nperks, upgrades, and reward multipliers,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 365040,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "everything is designed to make you stick with \nthe same carrier as much as possible. Thus, the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 369760,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only way for international carriers like Cathay \nPacific, EVA Air, Emirates, Singapore Airlines,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374560,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or ANA to win is to create a product gap so wide \nthat travelers would feel worth trading up for.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 380320,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If their in-flight experience and service was only \nmarginally better, then Americans would just stick  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385200,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the standard path of Delta, United, or American \nfor points and status. At the same time, the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 391280,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "home countries of these Asian airlines are tiny \ncompared to the United States. Singapore, Dubai,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 397120,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thailand, and Taiwan - with the exception of \nJapan, these don’t have the population, land mass,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 403280,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or need for domestic air travel. Without adequate \nlocal demand, their airlines have no choice but  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408560,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to build their businesses around international \ntravel and poach Westerners to fill planes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 411040,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As a result, the leading Asian airlines are \noverwhelmingly international-based business.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 415680,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a total 180 from the major U.S. airlines, \nwhich are all overwhelmingly domestic-based  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 420400,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in both passengers served and revenue generated. \nEven though China has the greatest number of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 424000,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "travelers and Europe has plenty of businesses, \nwinning over Americans is the fastest ticket  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429520,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to profit for non-U.S. airlines. For one, \nAmericans fly far more frequently than any  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434800,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "other demographic. When flying and driving \nare your only two options for transit,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439040,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you really have no choice but to jump on a plane. \nUltimately, infrastructure aside, Americans  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 444240,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "uniquely possess the disposable income, buying \npower, and willingness to splurge. Because all  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 448400,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the money in aviation is in the premium cabins, \nwhere a single business class seat generates more  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 453280,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "profit than the entire row of economy behind it, \neverything in this global market pushes non-U.S.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457760,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "carriers towards the same business strategy. \nUnless you can bank on billions in free credit  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461680,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "card revenue or fall back on a massive domestic \nmarket, you have to go up-market to win over  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 466320,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Americans, pull them away from their usual \ncarriers, and thrive as a standalone airline.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469280,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If that means serving a better steak, making a \ncomfier seat, and pouring an expensive champagne,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474640,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Asia’s leading airlines are more than willing \nto make these investments to close the sale."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478880,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Japan Airlines’s First Class boasts 43-inch \n4K screens, headphone-free audio systems,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 484160,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "multi-course Michelin-starred fine dining, \nalongside some of Japan’s rarest sake. ANA’s  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486480,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "business class offers some of the widest plane \nseats in the world, sliding privacy doors,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 490880,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and intricate kaiseki meals. Taiwan’s EVA Air \nserves food from Din Tai Fung, hands out free  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496880,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pajamas and amenities from renowned fashion \ndesigners, and provides lie-flat cabins.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 501360,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, Starlux perfumes first class cabins \nwith a custom signature scent, sources meals  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 506000,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from local Michelin-starred restaurants, and \noffers seats with built-in massagers designed  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509120,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to lower your blood pressure. Singapore Airlines \nis legendary for its lobster courses and suites,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 513520,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where every passenger gets their own bed and \narmchair. Cathay Pacific ups the ante with custom  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 519440,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lighting, luxury bedding, and freshly pulled \nespressos, lattes, and cappuccinos available  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 524800,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on-demand. Meanwhile in the Middle East, those in \nfirst class get to take hot showers in the air,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 529760,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "socialize over cocktails in an onboard bar, and \nsleep in floor-to-ceiling suites with unlimited  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 534400,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Dom Perignon and caviar. And over in Qatar \nAirways, cabins can be freely combined into  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 539600,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dining or meeting spaces. With a restaurant-style \nkitchen on every flight, passengers can order  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 541840,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "anything off the menu at any time. Every one \nof these airlines is renowned for legendary  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 546000,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "service delivered by meticulously trained cabin \ncrews made up of mostly young, attractive women."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 552240,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Collectively, they blow past the premium offerings \nof even the wealthiest American carriers. But in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 557680,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reality, these Asian airlines are not really \ncompeting against Delta One or United Polaris.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 563120,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "U.S. airlines operate under a completely \ndifferent set of incentives. They only need  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 567200,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to provide a premium product that’s compliant \nenough to satisfy corporate travel policies  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 571520,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and comfortable enough to prevent executives from \ncomplaining. This in turn has become the defining  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 576480,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "standard for the modern American business class \n- inconsistent service, mediocre food tossed  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 581920,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "onto cheap plastic, and the same bread as economy. \nFor them, business class is not about excellence,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 585760,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but instead doing just enough to win the corporate \ncontracts that lock thousands of employees into  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 590720,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their ecosystems. Investing millions on caviar, \ndesigner bedding, or better food has virtually no  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 595680,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ROI, especially when these carriers are already \nlosing billions anyways doing the bare minimum.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 601200,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thus, the true competition for Asian airlines is \nwith each other. They must outdo one another in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 606080,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "extravagance and hospitality to win over American \ntravelers in the rare instances they step outside  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 611280,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of their credit card ecosystems. And even though \nAmericans fly more than any other demographic,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 616160,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the majority of flights they do take are domestic. \nOnly 18% of Americans fly internationally every  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 621680,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "calendar year and only 6-8% of this group flies \nto Asia. This means that Asian airlines are all  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 627600,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "competing for the top 1% of this 1.5% to fill \ntheir premium cabins. In short, if credit cards  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 633520,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are the ace up the sleeve for U.S. airlines, then \nluxury is the only trump card for Asian airlines."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 639440,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet today, in-flight experience is no \nlonger enough. International carriers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 644000,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have invested billions to extend their brand and \nprestige into lounges and terminals. Singapore  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 649440,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Airlines's first class passengers get to \ndine on unlimited wagyu burgers, lobster,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 653920,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and champagne at Changi Airport. Cathay Pacific’s \nlounges are stocked with private cabanas,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 659280,
    "dDurationMs": 3851,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stone bathtubs, complimentary massage stations \nat Hong Kong International. Elite members get  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 663131,
    "dDurationMs": 1669,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to munch on noodles while valets steam press their \nclothes for free. Japan Airline’s lounge features  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 664800,
    "dDurationMs": 4145,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a dedicated sushi bar with handmade nigiri and \nself-serve sake. ANA offers made-to-order ramen,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 668945,
    "dDurationMs": 2815,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "latte art, and high-tech work pods. In Taipei, \nStarlux passengers get picked up in private cars,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 671760,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "escorted through their own immigration, and \nlounge in their own private villas. Meanwhile  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 676240,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "EVA Air operates multiple lounges, each \nwith their own theme and all with self-serve  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 681040,
    "dDurationMs": 1226,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Haagen Dazs. Qatar Airway’s first class lounge \nin Doha is a museum with private bedrooms,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 682266,
    "dDurationMs": 1814,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "jacuzzis, fine dining, and ancient Islamic \nartifacts. Emirates’s first class passengers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684080,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "get their own terminal where they can indulge \nin free, exclusive cigar lounges, spas, bars,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 688960,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and restaurants - all separated from the public \ncrowds of the main terminal. These amenities are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 694000,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all calculated investments by every carrier to woo \ntravelers before they’ve settled on an itinerary.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 699440,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In contrast, the lounges offered by U.S. \nairlines, whether domestic or international, are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 703920,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "overcrowded, cramped, and sad experiences built \naround buffets of frozen food and cheap alcohol.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 709280,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ironically, the most luxurious lounges in American \nairports today are not by the carriers themselves,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 714800,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but rather the very same credit card companies \nthat are keeping them alive in the first place."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 719600,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet the popular misconception is the only \nreason Asian airlines can only afford this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 722800,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "opulence because of endless subsidies from their \ngovernments. The argument goes that these lounges,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 728320,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cabins, services, and infrastructure are all \nvanity projects bankrolled by the state for the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 733200,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sole purpose of national prestige. As a result, \nthese Asian carriers are free to ignore profit  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 737760,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and operate without shareholder constraints in \nways that U.S. carriers can never avoid. But the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 742000,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reality is the exact opposite. Most Asian \ncarriers are not state-owned. With the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 746880,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exception of Singapore Airlines, Qatar, Etihad, \nand Emirates - the rest are all publicly traded,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 753360,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for-profit corporations. And broadly speaking, \nthese Asian carriers are all not just surviving,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 758560,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but instead thriving as the most profitable \nairlines in the world. Like their American peers,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 763440,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they all publicize their financials and are \nrequired to generate ROI. Any excess returns  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 766560,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "must be redistributed back to shareholders. \nUltimately, every government in the world  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 770640,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "provides some degree of financial backing \nand safety net for its domestic airlines,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 774960,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but no state can magically fill seats or \nmanufacture profits. From a business standpoint,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 780080,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the most important distinction of all is that \nthese airlines make money flying passengers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 784560,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whereas U.S. carriers depend entirely \non credit card revenue to survive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 788880,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there is a point where luxury becomes excess. \nThrough the 2010s, legacy U.S. airlines - Delta,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 795440,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "United, American - aggressively lobbied the Obama \nand Trump administrations to ban Emirates, Etihad,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 801360,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Qatar from American airports as unfair, \nstate-owned competition. They asserted that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 804400,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there was no way any airline could afford onboard \nshowers, cocktail bars, and unlimited caviar.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 809840,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These luxuries were only possible because of \nthe tens of billions of dollars that these  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 813760,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "oil states were pumping into their airlines. \nBacked by infinite public funds, these Middle  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 818560,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Eastern carriers were now flooding lucrative \ninternational routes with impossibly lower fares  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 825040,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and best-in-class experiences. The nuance here, \nhowever, is that U.S. airlines also receive  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 829920,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "significant government support. Like automakers, \nairlines are critical to economic sovereignty,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 835360,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "national security, and employment. A country \nwithout its own airlines would have to depend  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 839840,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on a foreign power to move citizens and commerce. \nObviously, this is an outcome that no superpower  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 845280,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would ever accept. Thus, the big airlines are \nmodern-day flag carriers for their countries, just  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 849680,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wrapped in private logos, and every one is \nbacked by their state in some way. In the U.S.,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854640,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "airlines don’t get free cash from the government \nbut instead are propped up by the tax code and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 858960,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "municipalities. In the 2000s, nearly every major \nU.S. airline filed for bankruptcy. Despite their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 864800,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "collapse, the planes were never grounded and \npassengers continued to fly. The airlines have to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 869840,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "use federal bankruptcy as a legal shield to dump \ntheir billion dollar liabilities onto taxpayers,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 875280,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tear up existing union contracts, force \n30% salary cuts onto their workforce, and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 880640,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "erase the billions owed to suppliers. This kind \nof bankruptcy protection would have been illegal  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 885360,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in any other nation. The U.S. government has also \ndone cash injections. The first was after 9/11,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 891280,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when Congress handed $5 billion dollars to U.S. \nairlines to keep them afloat during the subsequent  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 896240,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "slump when Americans were too scared to fly. The \nsecond was during the pandemic, when U.S. airlines  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 901840,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "collectively received $59 billion dollars \nso they could keep staff on payroll without  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 906240,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "having to dig into their own cash reserves. But \nat the end of the day, the greatest protectionism  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 910480,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exists only for those too big to fail. A low-cost \ncarrier like Spirit doesn’t get this protection,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 915600,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "simply because it’s too small to be worth saving. \nAt the same time, when an airline wants to build  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 920240,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a new fancy terminal for themselves, they get \nto tap into special low-interest financing. The  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 925440,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "municipality that owns the airport issues \ntax-exempt municipal bonds on behalf of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 929840,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the airline and then passes on public proceeds \nto fund the private construction. This cheap,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 934800,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "state-faciliated capital has funded most of \nthe mega terminal projects in the U.S. in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 939440,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the past decade. Ultimately, the greatest irony \nis that for all the money that the Middle East  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 944320,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has pumped into its airlines, these amounts still \ndon’t come close to the billions that legacy U.S.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 949360,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "carriers receive every year from credit cards.\n \nLike automakers, passenger aviation is not and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 954720,
    "dDurationMs": 1568,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will never be a free market. It’s not possible \nto simplify things down into a black and white  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 956288,
    "dDurationMs": 2992,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "state of private versus public. Across Asia, \ngovernments operate in deep alignment with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 959280,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their airlines - even in fully privatized markets \nlike Japan and Taiwan. For these small countries,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 964800,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a reputable, premium airline is a critical \ninstrument for economy and diplomacy. As a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 969280,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "city-state, Hong Kong is fueled entirely by \nservices - banking, trade, and tourism. The  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 973040,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "country has spent generations building up its \nstatus as the finance and logistics hub for Asia.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 978480,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cathay Pacific serves as that physical backbone \n- flying in overseas travelers, business leaders,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 983920,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lawyers, and power brokers to close deals while \nflying out goods made in China to the West. If an  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 989360,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "airline goes down, the entire country goes with \nit. As a result, the government is willing to do  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 994400,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "anything to keep its airline alive, even if that \nmeans breaking away from its strict laissez-faire  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 999520,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dogma. During the pandemic, Hong Kong injected \nbillions of public taxpayer funds to save the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1004480,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "private, for-profit carrier, marking the first \never government intervention in the country's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1008800,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "history since 1998. This symbiotic relationship \nmeans that Cathay Pacific forever remains the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1014640,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dominant airline at Hong Kong International \nwith the best real estate, gates, time slots,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1019680,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and lounges. The same dynamic is at play with \nSingapore. As another city state, Singapore has  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1025280,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "no natural resources. Thus, Singapore Airlines and \nChangi Airport function in tandem as a unified,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1031440,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "state-owned engine that anchors the nation \n- flying in the fresh food needed to feed  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1035920,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its citizens, attracting the foreign investment \nand corporate decision makers needed for growth,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1039200,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and flying out the high-value microchips \nmanufactured on the island. Singapore  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1044640,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Airlines’s legendary cabins are there not to \nimpress wealthy tourists as much as they are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1049440,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to persuade Fortune 500 executives to establish or \nmaintain regional offices on the island. All the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1052080,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "excess profits from the carrier get returned \nto the government in the form of dividends.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1055520,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Naturally, when the pandemic hit, the airline was \nimmediately granted a 14 billion dollar rescue  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1059600,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "package to keep staff employed, planes in \nthe air, and the entire economy humming. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1064160,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even in Japan, where all domestic airlines \nare fully private, for-profit ventures, ANA  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1068480,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and JAL operate closely in step with government \npriorities. While cars remain the country’s top  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1073440,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "export, tourism has surged in recent years to \nbecome the country’s second-largest contributor  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1077920,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to GDP. The historic depreciation of the yen has \nturned Japan into an affordable destination. With  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1084080,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "millions of tourists flooding in every year, \nANA and JAL are now regarded as critical growth  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1088960,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "engines that are injecting much-needed foreign \ncash into the country’s stagnant economy. The  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1093920,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Japanese government grants its domestic airlines \nthe best real estate and gates at its airports,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1099040,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and in return, those carriers help advance \nnational priorities—promoting rural Japan and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1104080,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "marketing travel packages designed to funnel \ntourist spend into regions beyond Tokyo. The  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1109600,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dynamic in Taiwan is totally different. \nThe country’s world-class semiconductor  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1113920,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "industry generates massive organic \ndemand for air freight and business  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1117680,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "travel. Tourism plays just a tiny role in the \nnation’s GDP. Silicon Valley executives will  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1119440,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fly to Taiwan for its chips and expertise by any \nmeans necessary. Because the nation’s economic  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1124720,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "value is rooted in critical technology, the \ncountry doesn’t need to rely on airlines to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1128800,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "project its prestige or drive foreign investment. \nAs a result, EVA Air and Starlux receive no public  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1135200,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "subsidies as for-profit entities and compete head \nto head alongside the state-owned China airlines. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1141120,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In Qatar, the boundary between airline and airport \ndoesn’t exist - both are fully state-owned assets  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1145920,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "controlled by the same leaders. As an fossil \nfuel state where natural gas exports make  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1150480,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "up 80% of its GDP, Qatar’s leaders understand \nbetter than anyone that its present-day riches  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1155680,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cannot not last. The country has aggressively \nreinvested its fortunes into building up Qatar  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1160880,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Airways in the hopes that the airline can drive \nthe country’s transformation away from oil and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1165600,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "towards finance and tourism. From this lens, \nQatar Airways is both the marketing muscle and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1171040,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the funnel that physically carries international \ncash and talent into Doha. In contrast,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1176160,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Dubai possesses little oil. With oil production \ndown since the 90s, the state recognized early  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1181440,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that its fortunes would not last and a new future \nof tourism, logistics, and trade would only be  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1185600,
    "dDurationMs": 14080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "possible through aviation. Emirates Airlines \nserves as a critical advertisement and pipeline  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1199680,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for international wealth - bringing in the wealthy \ntourists, foreign investors, and institutional  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1204000,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "capital that in turn fuel the city’s real estate. \nIn short, the smaller and less self-sufficient a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1209440,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nation, the more likely it will cultivate, \nfoster, and nurture a premium airline to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1214320,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "project its image and relevance on the world stage \nin the absence of hard military or economic power. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1219600,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the other hand, U.S. airlines are not treated \nas flag carriers. While they are still recognized  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1224880,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as critical national infrastructure, the federal \ngovernment treats United, Delta, and American  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1229840,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like private utility providers. Beyond safety and \nanti-trust, the U.S. remains hands-off. With an  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1236000,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "abundance of hard power and soft power as the \nglobal leader in military strength, currency,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1241600,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "banking, culture, and entertainment - the \ncountry has no strategic incentive to elevate  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1246080,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its airlines or infrastructure. America is a \nbrand-name destination. Tourists will visit,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1250800,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the wealthy will immigrate, and the talent will \ncome no matter how poor the in-flight experience  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1255680,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and onboard product gets. As we covered earlier, \nwithout high-speed rail, air travel in the U.S.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1257510,
    "dDurationMs": 730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is mostly domestic and Americans treat jumping on \na plane like hopping on a bus or train. Thus, the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1258240,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "overwhelming priority is punctuality and safety \nrather than aesthetics and experience. This  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1264000,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mindset bleeds into American airports where \nterminals have historically been designed for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1268320,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "efficiency rather than spectacle. As a result, \nmost U.S. airports languish far behind those of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1272960,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Asian countries with faded carpets, low ceiling, \ncramped spaces, and outdated lighting.Things  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1278960,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only changed in 2014 when Joe Biden said \nthe quiet part out loud as vice president,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1284480,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "describing New York LaGuardia as something out \nof a third world country. His viral comments and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1289520,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "efforts since have driven bipartisan investment. \nWhile a few American airports in recent years have  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1294000,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "begun to buck the trend like Portland and \nSFO, these award-winning upgrades took over  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1298080,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a decade to materialize, billions in funding, \nand remain limited to a handful of big cities.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1303600,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The core challenge is that American airports are \nrun by either a state agency, city government,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1308800,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "local airport or port authority, who must keep \ntheir lights on by charging fees to passengers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1312960,
    "dDurationMs": 4032,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and airlines, issuing bonds, or receiving federal \ngrants. They’re generally not taxpayer funded and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1316992,
    "dDurationMs": 2208,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are required to be self-sustaining enterprises. \nThis fragmentation in governance and funding  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1319200,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is the reason behind the extreme inconsistency \nof American airports and also generally limits  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1324240,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "renovations to cities where aviation is a \npolitical priority or is already thriving. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1329200,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because U.S. airports are not subsidized \nby taxpayers, they generally don’t have  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1333200,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the money lying around to fund billion-dollar \nterminal rebuilds and expansions on their own.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1337680,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As landlords, they have to rely on their tenant \nairlines to lead and finance renovations. For  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1344640,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "airports that are already dominated by a single \ncarrier, the path of least resistance is to let  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1349200,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that airline take even greater control over its \nown terminal and decide everything from the type  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1354160,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of chairs passengers sit in to the number of \ngates their planes get to park at. As we covered  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1359200,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the past on Modern MBA, the major U.S. airlines \nrule through fortresses. These are airports where  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1365040,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "United, Delta, or American single-handedly hold \n70% or more market share and physically block out  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1371360,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "competition by dominating the limited number of \ngates, ticket counters, and real estate available.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1376880,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Private carriers love this arrangement \nbecause it gives them leverage. For them,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1383120,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "terminal renovations aren’t just about making \nbigger, nicer spaces for planes and passengers,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1388160,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but about asserting control over the airport and \npassenger journey. The tension is that airports  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1391760,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are public facilities, built on public land, \nthat exist to benefit all travelers. Yet under  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1397200,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this model, public infrastructure gets warped \nto serve private interests and a terminal gets  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1401840,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "optimized for a single carrier, brand, and set \nof passengers rather than the general public it's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1407200,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meant to serve. Because the flashiest upgrades \ncost billions, this strategy is available only to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1412400,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the richest and biggest U.S. carriers. They're the \nonly ones with the cash flow and fortress hubs to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1417360,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "play this game in the first place. Thus, even if \na renovation runs over in both time and budget,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1422720,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the airline still comes out ahead every time as a \nnew terminal solidifies the airport's dependence  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1427200,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on it for the next few decades. It's a case where \nthe rich get richer and the poor get poorer.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1432480,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This also leads to inevitable fragmentation \nwithin a single airport, where a brand-new,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1436800,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "privately funded terminal will sit adjacent to \nanother with its outdated flooring, low ceilings,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1441760,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and basic amenities - simply because that \nrival airline chose not to invest in its space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1447120,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In contrast, Asian and Middle Eastern airports \noperate on a top-down model where the airport  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1452160,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "authority designs, expands, and renovates every \nterminal under a single unified aesthetic and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1457040,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "holistic passenger vision. Beyond the \nlounges, no control is ever ceded to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1460800,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an airline and even state-owned carriers must \noperate within the space provided. The airport  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1465840,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "funds everything itself and no tenant is allowed \nto control or overhaul a terminal the way U.S.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1470320,
    "dDurationMs": 921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "airlines do. When South Korea anticipated \nthat their airport was hitting capacity,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1471241,
    "dDurationMs": 83,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the state launched a multi-billion dollar \nexpansion to Incheon and handed the keys  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1471324,
    "dDurationMs": 2996,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the fully privatized Korean Air. Singapore \nproactively upgrades Changi airport to ensure  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1474320,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the infrastructure keeps up with the experience \nand product of their airline. And as Japan has  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1477520,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "expanded Tokyo Airport to accommodate the historic \nvolume of tourists, ANA and JAL have matched the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1480880,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "state’s ambitions in timing and scope by deploying \ntheir own capital to fill these new terminals with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1485360,
    "dDurationMs": 1109,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cutting-edge flagship lounges. Taiwan’s government \nhas initiated a $3 billion mega-project to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1486469,
    "dDurationMs": 107,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "proactively expand Taoyuan Airport so that EVA Air \nand Starlux have the space to build more check-in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1486576,
    "dDurationMs": 704,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lobbies and exclusive lounges. And as Emirates \nhas outgrown Dubai International, the city has  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1487280,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "committed $35 billion dollars to build a new,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1490000,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bigger, flashier international airport - \nand the same is happening for Qatar Airways."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1496160,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What’s notable is not just the timing and \ncoordination of these upgrades between airport  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1500320,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and airline, but that these massive capital \nprojects are ultimately financed by passengers.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1504960,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Asian countries bundle significant departure \nfees directly into every plane ticket based  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1509520,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on cabin class. Singapore collects $50 from every \npassenger in economy leaving Changi Airport, Hong  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1515760,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Kong collects $60, the Gulf states charges $40, \nand Japan takes $30. Now, the U.S. also charges  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1522960,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "departure fees but the vast majority of the fees \nget pocketed by the federal government, rather  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1527200,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than the airport. The Passenger Facility Charge \nis the only fee that flows to the airport and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1532240,
    "dDurationMs": 7360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has been capped at $4.50 for a direct domestic or \ninternational flight for the past 25 years. To put  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1539600,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into perspective just how asbsurdly low this is, \nTaipei International Airport collects more revenue  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1544480,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "per passenger than American airport. U.S. carriers \nhave successfully lobbied Congress for decades to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1550560,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "keep the Passenger Facility Charge low in order to \ndepress ticket prices, preserve the perception of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1555520,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "domestic air travel as affordable, and to stifle \npublic demand for high speed rail. In contrast,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1561120,
    "dDurationMs": 3601,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Asian airports keep the lion’s share of their \ndeparture fees as the charges are designed in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1564721,
    "dDurationMs": 1279,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the first place to fund their operations, rather \nthan skimmed by the state. As a result, American  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1566000,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "municipalities are starved of the income stream \nthat is meant to fund capital improvements for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1570640,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the airport in the first place. Thus, they have \nno choice but to rely on federal grants, tax-free  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1575040,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "municipal bonds, or private entities for upgrades. \nIt's ironic and difficult to believe, but under  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1578320,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this lens, U.S. airlines effectively strangle \nthe very airports they operate from. Meanwhile  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1583680,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in Asia, this divide between public-private \nor airport-airline just doesn’t exist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1588640,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What’s tricky about this kind of cross-border \nanalysis is that there are stark differences  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1592880,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in geography and scale. Cathay Pacific, Starlux, \nQatar, Emirates, ANA, etc. - Asian carriers get  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1595920,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to concentrate virtually all their investment and \neffort on one single airport - at most, two. If a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1601760,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "crisis occurs, the entire airline can mobilize and \nfunnel every penny of profit into perfecting their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1605360,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "crown jewel. In contrast, the major American \ncarriers must oversee a massive continental  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1610800,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "footprint. They each operate seven to 10 major \nhubs and serve hundreds airports nationwide,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1616160,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dozens of which also double as bases for crew, \nmaintenance, and parts. On any given day,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1621520,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they’re juggling a winter storm in New York, \na disruptive labor strike in San Francisco,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1625840,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a mechanical failure in Chicago, an unexpected \ncatering shortage in Los Angeles, or a scheduling  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1631040,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "error in Florida. With their fleet, staff, and \noperations spread out across hundreds of domestic  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1636560,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "venues, worrying about if the champagne at the \nlounge has been properly chilled is nowhere on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1641360,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the list of priorities. At the same time, while \nan Asian airline can unveil a world-class flagship  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1645920,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lounge at its lone hub in a single ribbon-cutting \nceremony, a U.S. carrier must split its resources  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1651120,
    "dDurationMs": 4298,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "across seven to ten different fortresses. They \nhave to peanut butter spread their capital for any  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1655418,
    "dDurationMs": 3862,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and every investment, which instantly dilutes \nany premium experience into a standardized,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1659280,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "replicable, watered-down product. Luxury is a \nfunction of exclusivity and personalization - yet  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1665600,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the sheer scale of American passenger aviation \nmakes delivering a bespoke service inherently  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1670800,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "difficult. United alone carries more passengers \nannually than Emirates and Singapore Airlines  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1675840,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "combined. And since most customers are flying \ndomestically, U.S. carriers use short-haul,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1680880,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "narrowbody workhorses like Boeing 737s and A320s. \nIn comparison, the international-centric Asian  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1683600,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "carriers all use spacious widebody long \nhaul aircraft that can seat hundreds. Thus,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1686960,
    "dDurationMs": 4439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "U.S. carriers operate with not just far more \nplanes, but the composition of the fleets are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1691399,
    "dDurationMs": 1961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dramatically different in size and type. The more \nplanes, the greater the workforce needed. They  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1693360,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "employ and oversee hundreds of thousands of flight \nattendants, baggage handlers, support agents,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1697600,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and mechanics spread across hundreds of hubs. \nMeanwhile, Asian airlines employ an order of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1702400,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "magnitude less and get to enjoy a workforce \nthat’s concentrated within their single  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1706000,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fortress. The fundamental difference in scale \nis why U.S. airline executives forever focus  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1710400,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on safety and on-time percentages as their north \nstar ahead of customer satisfaction and luxury."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1716560,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if we pause and look at all the concepts \ncovered, it seems like dominant Asian carriers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1720960,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shouldn’t need to compete on service as \nmuch as they do. They operate out of a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1724960,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "single state-protected fortress and \nget all the best real estate, gates,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1728480,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and time slots on home turf. If a traveler wants \na direct non-stop flight to Singapore, Taipei,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1734400,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tokyo, or Dubai with favorable arrival times, \nthey almost always have to fly the flag carrier.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1740000,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As long as the country is a popular destination, \nthe carrier on paper will always have business.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1744720,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the reality is that Asian carriers are locked \nin an endless global war with each other for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1748000,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "transit travelers - not just passengers whose \njourneys start or end at that country. Transit  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1753520,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "travelers are those with layovers or transfers \nwho only enter the country as a stepping stone  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1757200,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for their final destination. Since they’re just \nwaiting at the airport, they don’t inject the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1762320,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "same kind of capital into the local economy as \na tourist or businessman. But transit travelers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1769040,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are vital for international unit economics. There \nare simply not enough point-to-point travelers in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1772960,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "New York or San Francisco who want to fly to \nTokyo or Dubai to consistently fill a 400-seat  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1780240,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "plane every Tuesday. At the same time, those four \nand five figure business and first class cabins  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1783680,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only generate those great margins if the economy \nrows behind them are filled. From this lens,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1789120,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "economy is the floor that covers the flight’s \nfixed operating costs while premium cabins  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1793840,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "raise the ceiling - and an airline must fill \nout both sections to maximize profit. Thus,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1798960,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "transit traffic is essential to providing \nthe critical mass needed to fly the back of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1802880,
    "dDurationMs": 3663,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the plane and make these long-haul routes \neconomically viable in the first place."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1806543,
    "dDurationMs": 3137,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As a result, the leading Asian carriers have \nbeen so successful not only because of their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1809680,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in-flight experiences and airports, but also \nbecause they’re all located in countries  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1814400,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with unique geographic advantages that make \nthem good transit hubs in the first place.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1823200,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because China’s airspace is heavily restricted, \nHong Kong’s open skies stand out for business  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1827520,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and commerce. Cathay Pacific sweeps up \nregional passengers across East Asia and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1832480,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pools them all into single mega-flights to North \nAmerica. Singapore sits between two hemispheres,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1838000,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "making the country a natural gateway for \nlong-haul non-stop flights between West and South  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1842720,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Asia going across the Pacific and Indian Ocean. \nThe shortest flight path between North America  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1845360,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Asia is not a straight line across the Pacific \nOcean, but a curve that goes over Alaska. Japan is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1851120,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the first land mass that most trans-pacific planes \nhit along this route. As a result, JAL and ANA use  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1856480,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this geographical edge to capture transit traffic \nfrom North America heading to Southeast Asia and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1860400,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "vice versa. Taiwan sits at the midpoint between \nJapan and Southeast Asia, making it attractive for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1866000,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "transit passengers looking for a 2-4 hour hop to \nSoutheast Asia, rather than the 6 to 8 hour flight  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1871440,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that they would have to endure if their layover \nwas in Tokyo. Meanwhile, both EVA Air and Starlux  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1876240,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pool Southeast Asian traffic every afternoon \ninto waves of red-eye flights to the U.S."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1881600,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While the Asian airlines excel at the linear \ncorridors across the Pacific or Indian Ocean,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1886320,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Middle Eastern carriers sit at the literal \ncenter of the Afro-Eurasian landmass. Emirates,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1891120,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Qatar, and Etihad can connect virtually any city \npair on earth with a single-stop like China to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1896480,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Africa or Europe to India. At the same time, \nwhile Japan, Australia, and Europe shut down  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1901440,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their airports at night with strict curfews, \nthese barren Middle East airports and airlines  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1905600,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "keep flying 24/7. The only international routes \nthat the Gulf carriers don’t have an advantage in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1910800,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are the ones between the U.S. and East Asia - and \nthis lucrative corridor remains exclusive to ANA,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1916080,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "EVA Air, Cathay Pacific, Korean Air, and so on. \nTransit traffic is also invaluable because it  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1922000,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "unlocks cargo as a major revenue stream. \nSince these carriers all operate massive  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1926560,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "widebody aircraft, they can fit freight pallets \nand heavy shipments beneath the passengers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1931200,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they’re already carrying. They double as cargo \nbackbones for their countries and the transit  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1932550,
    "dDurationMs": 86,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "passengers they bring in generate billions \nin departure fees and duty-free concession  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1932636,
    "dDurationMs": 644,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spending each year—revenue that enriches their \nairports and fund future upgrades. Conversely,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1933280,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cargo is small fries for U.S. airlines. \nWith mostly narrow-body aircraft,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1937680,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there’s no space to accommodate heavy shipments. \nThe air cargo business that does exist has long  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1942640,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "been vacuumed up by dedicated giants like Fedex \nand UPS who offer better infrastructure, service,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1948880,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and expertise than what Delta, United, and \nAmerican could ever piece together. Ultimately,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1954240,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "success is not down to money alone, but rather the \ncombination of money and geography. A country that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1959520,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is not a popular destination or physically \non the way to a major market can build the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1963920,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "world’s most opulent airline or airport and \nstill fail. The Middle East carriers are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1968400,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thriving not because of their onboard showers \nor caviar service, but because planes that are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1972880,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "flying between Europe to Asia or Europe to \nAustralia naturally pass over the Gulf. They  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1978240,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tapped into the existing traffic overhead \nand used luxury to elevate their airlines."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1982720,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the end of the day, it’s a fly wheel. The more \nattractive a country becomes as a destination  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1987600,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or transit hub, the greater volume of passengers \nthat it can funnel through its airport. The more  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1993040,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "traffic through its airport, the more departure \nfees the venue gets to collect, and the greater  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1996560,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the likelihood that planes can be packed to \ncapacity. The higher the load factor, the lower  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2001280,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the operating costs, and the greater the margins \nfor the airline. This surplus then flows back into  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2006720,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the in-flight product and the infrastructure, \nwhich in turn fuels the airline’s profits,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2011120,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the airport’s revenues, the national economy, \nand the country’s standing on the world stage. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2016640,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because even transit travelers have a \nchoice of where to spend their layover,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2019760,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Asian countries and airlines must continually \nelevate their onboard experiences, lounges,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2024560,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and airports to ensure that their hub remains \nthe most compelling layover or destination."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2029520,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The final and perhaps most insurmountable divide \nbetween American and Asian airlines is labor.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2034400,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "U.S. carriers employ rigid, unionized workforces \nwho are protected from involuntary termination,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2040080,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "governed by strict work rules, and are \nguaranteed raises. Under this structure,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2042800,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the compensation and assignment is dictated \nby seniority rather than performance. This is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2047840,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why if you ride United or Delta’s business class, \nyou’ll generally end up with the oldest and most  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2052640,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "jaded flight attendants. Since flight assignments \nare determined by hire date, the most senior staff  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2058160,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lock down the most popular international flights \nto London, Paris, Tokyo, and so on for themselves.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2061840,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These routes allow them to complete their monthly \nflying quotas in just a few trips, maximize their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2066720,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "daily stipends, and enjoy company-paid layovers in \nluxury hotels. And since pay is based on tenure,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2074000,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there is no incentive to do anything beyond the \nbare minimum. Those who do go above and beyond  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2078560,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "don’t get rewarded as merit does not supersede \nseniority. To control these unavoidable labor  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2082800,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "costs, every U.S. airline staffs their airlines \nto the minimum required by law. In contrast,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2088400,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "leading Asian carriers generally overstaff their \nplanes well above the legal minimums to guarantee  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2093680,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "high-touch service and complete experience for all \ncabins. While being a flight attendant in the U.S.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2099680,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is seen as a stable middle class job with travel \nperks, being a flight attendant in Asia is a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2103840,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "coveted, prestigious service job that opens future \ndoors into corporate, retail, and banking. The  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2105760,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "applicant pool is ultra-competitive with training \nregiments that cover everything from grooming  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2110160,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and posture to presentation and emotional \nintelligence. Every carrier has uncompromising  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2115920,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "standards with employment structures and criteria \nthat would be illegal and discriminatory in the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2120560,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "West. Flight attendants are picked based on their \nage, fitness, and appearance. Most carriers hire  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2126480,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "crew on fixed 3-5 years contracts where only \nthe cream of the crop who pass the medical  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2131040,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "assessments, performance reviews, and visual \nevaluations get extended. Those who fail or  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2136400,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "simply age out get transitioned to back-office \nroles or must find a job in a different sector. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2141040,
    "dDurationMs": 4016,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While unions are banned in the Middle East, \nthey do exist across Asian carriers like Cathay  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2145056,
    "dDurationMs": 1184,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Pacific, Singapore Airlines, EVA Air, Korean \nAir, ANA, and JAL. However, their governments  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2146240,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "historically side with management during disputes \nas the airline is simply too vital to the economy  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2151200,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and country to be bogged down by collective \nbargaining. At the same time, the carriers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2155440,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "regularly hire crew from beyond their \nhome country, which enables them to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2158720,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "suppress salaries over time, widen recruitment to \nbillions of applicants, and foster competition,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2164240,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even for existing hires. In contrast, labor is \nthe single largest operating expense for Delta,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2169920,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "United, American, and Southwest. On top of \nthe day-to-day staff, each of these carriers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2175120,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "also must pay hundreds of millions every year to \nfund the retirement of their retirees. Meanwhile,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2180400,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because the leading Asian countries have \npublic healthcare and nationalized pensions,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2184320,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their carriers don’t have to carry billions \nof dollars in retirement liabilities the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2187520,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "same way that U.S. airlines do. This cost \nstructure enables foreign carriers to generate  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2194320,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "profits in ways that no American airline can - \ncapturing maximum spend from American travelers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2199840,
    "dDurationMs": 8960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in USD, paying their expenses in weaker local \ncurrencies, and reinvesting the remaining margin  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2208800,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into aircraft, infrastructure, and innovation.\nUltimately, the main ingredient behind all  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2214080,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of this is culture as there are plenty of \ncounter-examples. Not every Asian airline  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2216880,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is a success. And if we look at the big-name \nEuropean carriers like British Airways, Lufthansa,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2222400,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Air France, these are airlines with massive \nappeal, strong government backing, and geographic  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2228800,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "advantages. British Airways maintains a \nnear-monopoly over London Heathrow - the world’s  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2235840,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "second busiest international airport. The same is \ntrue for Lufthansa and Frankfurt. With the soft  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2242000,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "power of the UK and Germany, these two carriers \non paper have everything they need to match the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2247040,
    "dDurationMs": 5260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "success of leading Asian carriers. But in reality, \nthe in-flight experience, onboard product, and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2252300,
    "dDurationMs": 5940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "customer experience at these 2 European airlines \nlags behind even legacy U.S. airlines. Thus,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2258240,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "British Airways and Lufthansa are counter examples \nthat prove that even if you have a single fortress  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2263440,
    "dDurationMs": 7227,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hub, historic demand, and soft power - it means \nnothing if the underlying culture has stagnated."
    } ]
  } ]
}
